	('a94f987e-04de-485d-956d-687c4d6d649a', 'test-english-books-35', 'testing text', 'ISBN: 978-088141-876-7, 9780881418767 In On the Holy Spirit, Saint Basil the Great offers a powerful defense of the Church’s teaching on the Holy Spirit, showing the Spirit''s role in guiding believers and sustaining the life of the Church. This timeless work articulates the Orthodox understanding of the Trinity, emphasizing the Spirit’s equality with the Father and the Son. Praised by his friend Saint Gregory of Nazianzus as a "noble champion of the truth" and a "second Joseph" for his care for the needy, Basil’s wisdom and holiness shine through in this work. He combines theological depth with practical insights, encouraging readers to seek a deeper relationship with the Spirit through prayer, ascetic discipline, and acts of charity. Whether you’re new to Orthodox theology or seeking to enrich your spiritual life, On the Holy Spirit offers guidance for understanding the Spirit’s presence and working in both the Church and the individual believer’s heart. About the Author: Stephen M. Hildebrand is Assistant Professor of Theology at Franciscan University of Steubenville.', NULL, 53.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/5a6896b7-af11-4986-a14c-efc106068dcb.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:42:01.436914+00', '2026-09-19 12:42:01.436914+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('e2ab0eac-c179-4346-ae91-f67a926777ac', 'test-english-books-29', 'testing text', 'Popular Patristics Series Volume 44B ISBN:978-0-88141-427-1, 9780881414271 Discover the heart of Christian faith with On the Incarnation by Saint Athanasius, a foundational text that explains the mystery of God becoming human. Written in the 4th century, this masterpiece presents the core belief defended at the councils of Nicaea and Constantinople: that Christ, fully divine and fully human, came to restore our relationship with God, so that we may share in His divine life. With clarity and depth, Saint Athanasius explains why Jesus’ incarnation and resurrection are essential for salvation. This timeless work has shaped Christian theology across all traditions, making it a "must-read" for anyone seeking to deepen their understanding of Christ’s nature and mission. This edition features an introduction by C.S. Lewis, offering insights for readers from all backgrounds. Whether you are Orthodox, Protestant, Catholic, or exploring Christianity, this book will leave you with a richer understanding of Christ’s transformative love and how it invites us into communion with God. About the Translator: The V. Rev. Dr John Behr was Dean and Professor of Patristics at St. Vladimir''s Orthodox Theological Seminary. He is Editor of the Popular Patristics Series. Other SVS Press books by Fr John are The Way to Nicaea , The Nicene Faith (2 vols.), The Mystery of Christ , The Cross Stands While the World Turns , and Becoming Human ,', NULL, 50.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/d50acc24-bd52-4303-98c5-b57d9dbc1fe7.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:41:14.460212+00', '2026-09-19 12:41:14.460212+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
