	('9e127830-384c-4147-9177-656c9021c00b', 'test-english-books-4', 'testing text', 'ISBN: 978-088141-876-7, 9780881418767 In On the Holy Spirit, Saint Basil the Great offers a powerful defense of the Church’s teaching on the Holy Spirit, showing the Spirit''s role in guiding believers and sustaining the life of the Church. This timeless work articulates the Orthodox understanding of the Trinity, emphasizing the Spirit’s equality with the Father and the Son. Praised by his friend Saint Gregory of Nazianzus as a "noble champion of the truth" and a "second Joseph" for his care for the needy, Basil’s wisdom and holiness shine through in this work. He combines theological depth with practical insights, encouraging readers to seek a deeper relationship with the Spirit through prayer, ascetic discipline, and acts of charity. Whether you’re new to Orthodox theology or seeking to enrich your spiritual life, On the Holy Spirit offers guidance for understanding the Spirit’s presence and working in both the Church and the individual believer’s heart. About the Author: Stephen M. Hildebrand is Assistant Professor of Theology at Franciscan University of Steubenville.', NULL, 53.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/f0098330-003f-46d1-9073-d432c948912c.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:39:30.577265+00', '2026-09-19 12:39:30.577265+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
