	('61c3e9a7-c9e6-44db-bdfe-d1a5b1539689', 'test-st-shenouda-press-4', 'testing text', 'Step into the rich and vivid world of ancient Israel, where the life and ministry of Jesus unfolded over two thousand years ago. In this compelling book, you’ll embark on a journey back in time, exploring the customs, traditions, and rituals that shaped the lives of His people—particularly the ancient Jewish wedding traditions. Through these cultural insights, you will gain a profound understanding of the love story at the heart of salvation: Christ, the Bridegroom, and His church, the bride. One of the key elements woven into this exploration is the ancient text of the Song of Songs. In this poetic book, “Jehovah,” the Loving Bridegroom, pours out His heart toward His beloved bride. Skeptics may view the Song of Songs merely as a collection of romantic poems between a husband and wife. According to ancient Jewish tradition the Jews understood the Song of Songs as a figurative narrative expressing the love of God, the Bridegroom, for His bride, Israel. This rich tradition offers deep insight into the relationship between God and His people, a relationship that reaches its ultimate fulfillment in Christ’s love for the church. The author invites you to see Jesus Christ in a new and intimate light by drawing connections between these ancient wedding customs and the mystery of Christ’s relationship with His followers. Just as the Jewish Bridegroom prepared and pursued his bride, Christ, our Bridegroom, prepares and pursues the church with divine love and devotion. Through this powerful metaphor, you will come to a greater appreciation of the depth and beauty of the salvation story. But the book goes beyond mere history or cultural exploration—it offers a fresh perspective on essential aspects of Christian life. By delving into the symbolism of the Jewish wedding and the timeless truths of the Song of Songs, the author provides new insights into the seven sacraments of the church, as well as the practices of prayer, fasting, Bible study, and marriage. Each of these elements is illuminated in the light of Christ’s love, helping you to see how they fit into His grand plan of redemption. The sacraments, often viewed as mere rituals, come to life in these pages as expressions of a deeper mystery: the divine union between Christ and His people. As you read, you will begin to see Christ not only as Creator and Savior but as the loving Bridegroom who desires an intimate and eternal relationship with His bride—the church. Ultimately, this book is an invitation to enter into a deeper relationship with Jesus Christ, to see Him not only as Lord and Savior but as the Bridegroom who calls each of us to be part of His eternal bride. Through prayer, reflection, and a fresh look at familiar traditions, you’ll be inspired to embrace the fullness of your faith and experience the transformative power of Christ’s love. Are you ready to begin this journey? Step back to where the story began and discover the magnificent mystery of the Divine Bridegroom. Author: Bishoy Boulos ISBN : 978-1-7635450-9-0 Publisher Name : St Shenouda Press Publisher URL : www.stshenoudapress.com Publication Year : 2024 Pages :', NULL, 12.00, 'St Shenouda Press', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/19194ab3-6f8b-467d-89da-606e52085171.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 13:15:08.312623+00', '2026-09-19 13:15:08.312623+00', '{"St Shenouda Press"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
