	('5528d382-fb85-4a35-9359-20e6a626c326', 'test-english-books-23', 'testing text', 'ISBN: 978-088141-876-7, 9780881418767 In On the Holy Spirit, Saint Basil the Great offers a powerful defense of the Church’s teaching on the Holy Spirit, showing the Spirit''s role in guiding believers and sustaining the life of the Church. This timeless work articulates the Orthodox understanding of the Trinity, emphasizing the Spirit’s equality with the Father and the Son. Praised by his friend Saint Gregory of Nazianzus as a "noble champion of the truth" and a "second Joseph" for his care for the needy, Basil’s wisdom and holiness shine through in this work. He combines theological depth with practical insights, encouraging readers to seek a deeper relationship with the Spirit through prayer, ascetic discipline, and acts of charity. Whether you’re new to Orthodox theology or seeking to enrich your spiritual life, On the Holy Spirit offers guidance for understanding the Spirit’s presence and working in both the Church and the individual believer’s heart. About the Author: Stephen M. Hildebrand is Assistant Professor of Theology at Franciscan University of Steubenville.', NULL, 53.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/c12c0da7-f043-42d8-a5f2-91f59fa0dfe3.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:40:46.055715+00', '2026-09-19 12:40:46.055715+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('e7d22d87-1f22-4c6f-a2e9-37fb51c98430', 'test-english-books-28', 'testing text', 'ISBN: 978-0-913836-04-0, 9780913836040 In Great Lent, Fr. Alexander Schmemann offers profound insights into the rich spiritual meaning of the Lenten season. Exploring treasures like the Liturgy of the Presanctified Gifts, the Prayer of St. Ephraim, and the Canon of St. Andrew, this revised edition unveils the depth and purpose of Lenten worship, often misunderstood or overlooked. Schmemann describes Lent as a journey of “bright sadness,” a time to awaken our hearts to the remembrance of Christ and rekindle a relationship with God that may feel distant. Through fasting, prayer, and reflection, Lent becomes a sacred space for spiritual renewal, leading us through its solemnity to the radiant joy of the Resurrection. This book is an inspiring companion for anyone seeking to experience Lent more deeply, rediscover the beauty of Orthodox worship, and draw closer to God during this transformative season. About the Author: Fr Alexander Schmemann was a prolific writer, brilliant lecturer, and dedicated pastor. Former dean and professor of liturgical theology at St Vladimir''s Orthodox Theological Seminary, his insight into contemporary culture and liturgical celebration left an indelible mark on the Christian community worldwide.', NULL, 50.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/4ee31101-3371-45d6-9687-4b216c1aff1e.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:41:06.743629+00', '2026-09-19 12:41:06.743629+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('94ca12db-a98e-4ca0-be81-526c6e688e7f', 'test-english-books-8', 'testing text', 'Popular Patristics Series Volume 44B ISBN:978-0-88141-427-1, 9780881414271 Discover the heart of Christian faith with On the Incarnation by Saint Athanasius, a foundational text that explains the mystery of God becoming human. Written in the 4th century, this masterpiece presents the core belief defended at the councils of Nicaea and Constantinople: that Christ, fully divine and fully human, came to restore our relationship with God, so that we may share in His divine life. With clarity and depth, Saint Athanasius explains why Jesus’ incarnation and resurrection are essential for salvation. This timeless work has shaped Christian theology across all traditions, making it a "must-read" for anyone seeking to deepen their understanding of Christ’s nature and mission. This edition features an introduction by C.S. Lewis, offering insights for readers from all backgrounds. Whether you are Orthodox, Protestant, Catholic, or exploring Christianity, this book will leave you with a richer understanding of Christ’s transformative love and how it invites us into communion with God. About the Translator: The V. Rev. Dr John Behr was Dean and Professor of Patristics at St. Vladimir''s Orthodox Theological Seminary. He is Editor of the Popular Patristics Series. Other SVS Press books by Fr John are The Way to Nicaea , The Nicene Faith (2 vols.), The Mystery of Christ , The Cross Stands While the World Turns , and Becoming Human ,', NULL, 50.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/a94a2d18-4a32-4066-a55a-5b9b68096a2c.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:40:02.60097+00', '2026-09-19 12:40:02.60097+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('a2b5f550-dbbc-47bd-9ad7-c724ac7268a5', 'test-english-books-3', 'testing text', 'In the second half of the fourth century the mystery of the Holy Spirit was the subject of fierce debate. Those who fought against the Nicene Creed opposed the idea that the Spirit was God. Even some of those willing to accept the equality of the Father and the Son saw the Spirit as more angelic than divine. This volume offers new translations of two of the most powerful Patristic reflections on the work and nature of the Holy Spirit. The first great testament to the Spirit''s divinity &#8212; showing how the Spirit creates and saves inseparably with the Father and the son &#8212; is St. Athanasius'' Letters to Serapion. Only a few years later, Didymus the Blind penned his own On the Holy Spirit, which is here translated into English for the first time. For Didymus, the Spirit transforms Christians by drawing them into the divine life itself, and must therefore be one with the Father and Son. About the Translators: Mark DelCogliano teaches at the University of St Thomas in St Paul, Minnesota. Andrew Radde-Gallwitz teaches at Loyola University, Chicago. Lewis Ayres teaches at Durham University in the United Kingdom.', NULL, 50.00, 'English Books', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/d3d04cde-e728-4231-8e6d-615a65a689b2.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:39:35.874956+00', '2026-09-19 12:39:35.874956+00', '{"English Books"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('e879aff5-5141-4667-aee3-650df7085f19', 'test-kids-activities-11', 'testing text', 'Fan with light and different speed with Christmas Logo', NULL, 15.00, 'Kids Activities', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/08501bfd-5288-4b14-8f4f-1de1f8de0942.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:52:37.30788+00', '2026-09-19 12:52:37.30788+00', '{"Kids Activities"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('e8859166-1814-4bd1-a8c3-f61f62f9b898', 'test-icons-frames-94', 'testing text', 'Hand made Golden Wooden Frame 30x40cm', NULL, 235.00, 'Icons & Frames', 5, 'https://mckglenrypsuahbsslgf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/trinity-media/products/bf08ace0-e8ff-4fc3-a985-5c7de1c7a2fa.png', false, true, '2026-09-19 12:49:32.709624+00', '2026-09-19 12:49:32.709624+00', '{"Icons & Frames"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
